# =============================================================================
# Vuelta — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development:   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored. This file is committed.
# =============================================================================
#
#  ⚠  NOTHING SECRET GOES IN THIS FILE. Not "nothing secret yet" — nothing, ever.
#
#  WHY THIS IS A HARD RULE, NOT A PREFERENCE:
#
#  electron-vite does not read these at runtime. It INLINES them into the
#  JavaScript bundle at build time. Any value here is baked into `out/` and
#  shipped inside the installer as readable text. `strings` on the binary, or
#  simply opening the bundle in a text editor, reveals it.
#
#  Worse, the bare `VITE_` prefix is exposed to the RENDERER, which is the
#  sandboxed, least-trusted process in the app.
#
#    MAIN_VITE_*      -> inlined into the main process bundle
#    PRELOAD_VITE_*   -> inlined into the preload bundle
#    RENDERER_VITE_*  -> inlined into the renderer bundle
#    VITE_*           -> inlined into ALL THREE, renderer included
#
#  Treat every value here as public. `npm run security:check` enforces this.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  WHERE THE ACTUAL SENSITIVE VALUES LIVE  (none of them are here, by design)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  Spotify Client ID    Not secret. A per-user runtime setting in
#                       %APPDATA%\Vuelta\config.json, entered on the setup
#                       screen. Each user brings their own — that is the whole
#                       distribution model. Hardcoding it here would break it.
#
#  Client secret        Does not exist. Vuelta uses Authorization Code with
#                       PKCE precisely because a desktop binary cannot keep a
#                       secret. There is nothing to store.
#
#  PKCE code verifier   Main-process memory only, for the lifetime of one auth
#                       attempt. Never written to disk.
#
#  Access token         Main-process memory only. Never crosses IPC to the
#                       renderer, never touches disk.
#
#  Refresh token        %APPDATA%\Vuelta\session.bin, encrypted with Electron
#                       safeStorage (Windows DPAPI, bound to your OS account).
#                       If encryption is unavailable it is NOT persisted at all
#                       rather than written in plain text.
#
#  See SECURITY.md for the full model.
#
# =============================================================================
#  Development-only toggles. Safe to be public. Ignored in packaged builds.
# =============================================================================

# Open Chromium DevTools automatically on launch. Dev builds only — this is
# force-disabled when the app is packaged, regardless of what is set here.
MAIN_VITE_OPEN_DEVTOOLS=false
